g milk and meat production and nitrogen utilisation efficiency. Gut Microbes. 2019;10:115&#x2013;32.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1080/19490976.2018.1505176</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6546327</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">30207838</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Hess MK, Hodgkinson HE, Hess AS, Zetouni L, Budel JCC, Henry H, et al. Large-scale analysis of sheep rumen metagenome profiles captured by reduced representation sequencing reveals individual profiles are influenced by factors associated with the environment and genetics of the host. BMC Genomics. 2023;24:551.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1186/s12864-023-09660-3</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC10506323</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">37723422</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Rowe SJ, Kittelmann S, Pinares-Pati&#xf1;o CS, Wood GR, Dodds KG, Kirk MR, et al. BRIEF COMMUNICATION: Genetic control of the rumen microbiome in sheep. Proc N Z Soc Anim Prod. 2015;75:67&#x2013;9.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Wallace RJ, Sasson G, Garnsworthy PC, Tapio I, Gregson E, Bani P, et al. A heritable subset of the core rumen microbiome dictates dairy cow productivity and emissions. Sci Adv. 2019;5:eaav8391.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1126/sciadv.aav8391</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6609165</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">31281883</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Zhang Q, Difford G, Sahana G, L&#xf8;vendahl P, Lassen J, Lund MS, et al. Bayesian modeling reveals host genetics associated with rumen microbiota jointly influence methane emission in dairy cows. ISME J. 2020;14:2019&#x2013;33.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/s41396-020-0663-x</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC7368015</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">32366970</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Mart&#xe