 &#xa0;Z, Shao &#xa0;N, Akinyemi &#xa0;T &#xa0;et al. &#xa0;Methanogenesis. Curr Biol. 2018;28:R727&#x2013;R32.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">29990451</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Mach &#xa0;V, Blaser &#xa0;MB, Claus &#xa0;P &#xa0;et al. &#xa0;Methane production potentials, pathways, and communities of methanogens in vertical sediment profiles of river Sitka. Front Microbiol. 2015;6:506.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC4440369</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">26052322</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Michoud &#xa0;G, Kohler &#xa0;TJ, Ezzat &#xa0;L &#xa0;et al. &#xa0;The dark side of the moon: first insights into the microbiome structure and function of one of the last glacier-fed streams in Africa. R Soc Open Sci. 2023;10:230329.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC10410210</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">37564072</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Michoud &#xa0;G, Peter &#xa0;H, Busi &#xa0;SB &#xa0;et al. &#xa0;Mapping the metagenomic diversity of the multi-kingdom glacier-fed stream microbiome. Nat Microbiol. 2025;10:217&#x2013;30.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">39747693</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Milner &#xa0;AM, Khamis &#xa0;K, Battin &#xa0;TJ &#xa0;et al. &#xa0;Glacier shrinkage driving global changes in downstream systems. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA. 2017;114:9770&#x2013;8.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5603989</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">28874558</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Nagler &#xa0;M, Praeg &#xa0;N, Niedrist &#xa0;GH &#xa0;et al. &#xa0;Abundance and biogeography of methanogenic and methanotrophic microorganisms across European streams. J Biogeogr. 2021;48:947&#x2013;60.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Nold &#xa0;SC, Zajack &#xa0;HA, Biddanda &#xa0;BA. Eukaryal and archaeal diversity