ydrogen underground storage</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">methanogenesis</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">salt caverns</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">sulphate reducing microbes</Keyword></KeywordList><CoiStatement>Silvan Hoth and Janiche Beeder are employed by Equinor, which is researching hydrogen storage in salt caverns. The other authors declare no conflicts of interest.</CoiStatement></MedlineCitation><PubmedData><History><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="revised"><Year>2024</Year><Month>11</Month><Day>24</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="received"><Year>2024</Year><Month>5</Month><Day>2</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="accepted"><Year>2024</Year><Month>12</Month><Day>2</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="medline"><Year>2025</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>13</Day><Hour>6</Hour><Minute>28</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pubmed"><Year>2025</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>13</Day><Hour>6</Hour><Minute>27</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="entrez"><Year>2025</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>13</Day><Hour>1</Hour><Minute>33</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pmc-release"><Year>2025</Year><Month>3</Month><Day>12</Day></PubMedPubDate></History><PublicationStatus>ppublish</PublicationStatus><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">40077886</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC11903319</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1111/1758-2229.70064</ArticleId></ArticleIdList><ReferenceList><Reference><Citation>Anisimova, M. , and Gascuel O.. 2006. &#x201c;Approximate Likelihood&#x2010;Ratio Test for Branches: A Fast, Accurate, and Powerful Alternative.&#x201d; Systematic Biology 55: 539&#x2013;552.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">16785212</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Alcaide, M. , Stogios P. J., Lafraya A., et&#xa0;al. 2015. &#x201c;Pressure Adaptation is Linked to Thermal Adaptation in Salt&#x2010;Saturated Marine Habitats.&#x201d; Environmental Micr