39, PMID:</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.3389/fmicb.2017.01339</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5513909</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">28769904</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Whiticar M. J. (1999). Carbon and hydrogen isotope systematics of bacterial formation and oxidation of methane. Chem. Geol. 161, 291&#x2013;314. doi: 10.1016/S0009-2541(99)00092-3</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/S0009-2541(99)00092-3</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Whiticar M. J., Faber E., Schoell M. (1986). Biogenic methane formation in marine and freshwater environments, CO<sub>2</sub> reduction vs. acetate fermentation&#x2014;isotope evidence. Geochim. Cosmochim. Acta
